  "article_opening": "Singapore Seizes $42M Mansion in Nvidia Chip Smuggling Probe\nJuly 2, 2026 -- Today’s top stories: Singapore Seizes $42M Mansion in Nvidia Chip Smuggling Probe, Rubio Would Step Aside for Vance in 2028 White House Race, and Google Ordered To Pay Klarna $1.97b in Antitrust Damages.\nBy CommonWealth Magazine\nSingapore seizes $42m home in Nvidia chip smuggling case\nSingapore authorities have seized a multimillion-dollar mansion and charged people with money laundering as part of a case of suspected c",
  "passage": "…leged that Google was giving preferential treatment to its own price-comparison service in its search results. The case relates to Google’s actions in Pricerunner markets in the UK, Sweden, and Denmark between 2008 and 2023.\nThe antitrust damages mark a partial win for Klarna, which had sought “ significantly higher ” compensation of close to $8Bn, the court said on Wednesday.\n“ Pricerunner is considered to have suffered damage as a result of Google having illegally favoured its price comparison service for many years, ” the Stockholm Patent and Market Court said in a statement. The case relates to Google’s actions in Pricerunner markets in the UK, Sweden, and Denmark between 2008 and 2023.\nSouth Korea to Invest Nearly $1.2 Trillion in Chips and AI Data Centers",
